    <string name="brp_osc_layout_classic">Classic</string>
    <string name="brp_osc_layout_pad_note">Like a modern controller: left stick at the top left, D-pad below it, buttons at the top right, right stick below them. For most games.</string>
    <string name="brp_osc_layout_fps_note">Shooters: a big movement stick low on the left, aim (LT) above it; aim stick, fire (RT) and a big jump (A) under the right thumb; L3 and R3 as buttons for sprint and melee.</string>
    <string name="brp_osc_layout_race_note">Racing: a big steering stick on the left, brake (LT) and a bigger accelerator (RT) as pedals on the right, LB/RB to shift gears. No right stick.</string>
    <string name="brp_osc_layout_fight_note">Fighting and arcade games: a big D-pad and two rows of large buttons (X Y RB over A B RT), LB and LT on top. No sticks.</string>
    <string name="brp_osc_layout_classic_note">Moonlight\'s original layout, with the changes you saved in it.</string>
